CommitProof mutant M3 — gateway-retry-any (CONTRACT §9.2, ADR-0007)

Intent: classifyError
(go/services/multigateway/poolergateway/pooler_gateway.go:96) returns
actionBuffer for every error on a PRIMARY target, including errors raised
after the statement began executing, so withBuffering waits for the
failover and executes the statement again on the new primary.
Failure mode modelled: unsafe retry — the gateway may buffer and replay only
errors that prove the statement did not run (no writable primary, MTF01,
pre-execution unavailable, 25006 / recovery 0A000 for a replay-safe
request, S14); replaying a statement whose first execution may have
committed executes it twice.
Sources: S14.
Detection (§9.2, ADR-0030): directed schedule D3 (profile buffered; W1
autocommit appends and W4 at 2× pacing; F2a on the leader three times, 15 s
after each heal); expected C3 duplicate-elements (an autocommit append
executed twice) or C2 g1a (a ledger insert reported failed with 23505 on
the retry while the first execution's row is present).
Function touched: classifyError (one function).

